    "progressSummary": "COMPLETE: Gallery entry submitted as PR #15499. 0 axioms, 0 sorries, 272 lines, 21 theorems. minFoldLevel characterized as index of largest prime factor.",
    "builtItems": [
      "constructible_mono_le: generalized monotonicity k \u2264 k \u2192 IsKFoldConstructible d k \u2192 IsKFoldConstructible d k",
      "constructible_mul_iff: IsKFoldConstructible(m*n) k \u2194 both factors are k-fold constructible",
      "minFoldLevel: Nat.find of foldLevelExists gives the minimum valid fold level",
      "minFoldLevel_le_iff: minFoldLevel(d) \u2264 k \u2194 IsKFoldConstructible d k (complete characterization)",
      "minFoldLevel_nth_prime: minFoldLevel(p_j) = j for j \u2265 1",
      "minFoldLevel_mul: minFoldLevel(m*n) = max(minFoldLevel m, minFoldLevel n)",
      "minFoldLevel_unbounded: \u2200 K, \u2203 d, minFoldLevel d > K",
      "Concrete values: 1\u21921, 2\u21921, 3\u21921, 5\u21922, 6\u21921, 7\u21923, 10\u21922, 11\u21924, 14\u21923, 15\u21922, 42\u21923",
      "Gallery entry: src/data/proofs/angle-trisection-oq-05-oq-03/ (meta.json, annotations.json, index.ts)",
      "PR #15499: research/angle-trisection-oq-05-oq-03 branch"
    ],
    "insights": [
      "minFoldLevel(d) = prime-sequence index of the largest prime factor of d",
      "minFoldLevel is multiplicative: minFoldLevel(m*n) = max(minFoldLevel m, minFoldLevel n)",
      "minFoldLevel is unbounded: for any K, the (K+1)-th prime requires K+1 folds",
      "Key technique: Nat.find over existential foldLevelExists gives the classical minimum",
      "Nat.nth_strictMono on the prime set gives monotonicity of foldPrimeBound",
      "minFoldLevel_mul: minFoldLevel(m*n) = max(minFoldLevel m, minFoldLevel n) \u2014 uses Nat.Prime.dvd_mul",
      "minFoldLevel_nth_prime: minFoldLevel(p_j) = j for j >= 1 \u2014 proved from OQ02 completeness theorems",
      "minFoldLevel_unbounded: no fixed k suffices for all degrees \u2014 proved by constructing p_{k+1}"
    ],
